WeightValue":700}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" No. It has ","decorations":[]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"no official status","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" in India or anywhere else, and it is not a holiday.","decorations":[]}}],"style":{"paddingTop":"0px","paddingBottom":"10px"},"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"JUSTIFY","lineHeight":"1.5"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"vh75h340","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Q. When is National Siblings Day?","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700}]}}],"style":{"paddingTop":"0px","paddingBottom":"10px"},"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"JUSTIFY","lineHeight":"1.5"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"qetx1342","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"A. 10 April","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":", a fixed date. It was founded by Claudia Evart in 1995 and named for her late sister Lisette's birthday.","decorations":[]}}],"style":{"paddingTop":"0px","paddingBottom":"10px"},"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"JUSTIFY","lineHeight":"1.5"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"in7me345","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Q. Who can you celebrate Sisters Day with?","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700}]}}],"style":{"paddingTop":"0px","paddingBottom":"10px"},"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"JUSTIFY","lineHeight":"1.5"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"7wv93347","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"A.","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" Anyone you consider a sister. It is commonly marked with ","decorations":[]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"biological sisters, cousins, sisters in law and close friends","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":".","decorations":[]}}],"style":{"paddingTop":"0px","paddingBottom":"10px"},"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"JUSTIFY","lineHeight":"1.5"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"jojhu351","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Q. How is Sisters Day celebrated?","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700}]}}],"style":{"paddingTop":"0px","paddingBottom":"10px"},"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"JUSTIFY","lineHeight":"1.5"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"o0sud353","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"A.","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" Usually with a message or social media post, a call, a small gift, or time spent together. There is no fixed way to observe it.","decorations":[]}}],"style":{"paddingTop":"0px","paddingBottom":"10px"},"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"JUSTIFY","lineHeight":"1.5"}}}],"documentStyle":{}},"contentText":"National Sisters Day 2027 falls on Sunday, 1 August. The date moves each year because the day is observed on the first Sunday of August rather than on a fixed date. It is not a public holiday and has no official standing anywhere. It grew out of American greeting card and social media culture and spread from there, and it is now widely marked in India too, usually with a post, a message or a small gift. National Sisters Day dates Year Date Day 2026 2 August 2026 Sunday (already passed) 2027 1 August 2027 Sunday 2028 6 August 2028 Sunday 2029 5 August 2029 Sunday Where the day comes from There is no founding charter or single originator that can be verified the way there is for Siblings Day. National Sisters Day is best understood as a modern social observance, popularised through greeting cards, retail promotions and then social media, rather than something declared by a government or institution. The vagueness is part of why the day works. It covers biological sisters, cousins, sisters in law, and the friends people call sisters without any of the ritual structure that a traditional festival would impose. Sisters Day, Siblings Day and Raksha Bandhan These three get confused constantly, so here is the difference. Occasion When What it marks National Sisters Day First Sunday of August. 1 August 2027 The bond between sisters. Modern, informal, no rituals. National Siblings Day 10 April, fixed All siblings. Founded by Claudia Evart in 1995, on her late sister Lisette's birthday. Raksha Bandhan Shravana Purnima, July or August A sister ties a rakhi on her brother's wrist and he pledges protection. An ancient Indian festival with a full ritual. Bhai Dooj Two days after Diwali The other Indian brother and sister festival, marked with a tilak and a shared meal.   The key distinction: Raksha Bandhan and Bhai Dooj are between brothers and sisters. Sisters Day is between sisters. Wishes and messages for your sister Short and warm •       Happy Sisters Day to the one person who has known every version of me. •       You were my first friend and you are still my best one. Happy Sisters Day. •       Thank you for taking my side even when I was wrong. Happy Sisters Day. •       Nobody makes me laugh like you do. Happy Sisters Day. For a sister who lives far away •       Different cities, same bond. Missing you today. Happy Sisters Day. •       Distance has not changed a thing between us. Happy Sisters Day. •       Wishing I could annoy you in person today. Happy Sisters Day. For an older sister •       You went first at everything so I would know how. Thank you for that. •       Half of what I know I learnt by watching you. Happy Sisters Day. For a younger sister •       Watching you grow up has been the best part of growing up myself. •       You are braver than I was at your age. Happy Sisters Day. For a friend who is like a sister •       We are not related and it has never mattered. Happy Sisters Day. •       Family is not only the people you are born to. Happy Sisters Day. Gift ideas for Sisters Day •       A photo of the two of you, printed and framed. Almost nobody prints photos any more, which is what makes it work. •       Something she has mentioned wanting and not bought for herself. •       A handwritten letter, especially if the two of you usually communicate in one line texts. •       A subscription to something she uses, such as an audiobook or streaming service. •       A shared plan rather than an object. A meal out, a day trip, a call blocked out with nothing else scheduled. •       For a sister who lives away, something from home that she cannot get where she is. Frequently asked questions about National Sisters Day Q. When is National Sisters Day 2027? A. Sunday, 1 August 2027. It is observed on the first Sunday of August, so the date changes each year. Q. Is National Sisters Day the same as Raksha Bandhan? A. No. Raksha Bandhan is an Indian festival between a brother and sister involving the tying of a rakhi. National Sisters Day is an informal modern observance between sisters, with no rituals attached. Q. Is National Sisters Day a public holiday? A. No. It has no official status in India or anywhere else, and it is not a holiday. Q. When is National Siblings Day? A. 10 April, a fixed date. It was founded by Claudia Evart in 1995 and named for her late sister Lisette's birthday. Q. Who can you celebrate Sisters Day with? A. Anyone you consider a sister. It is commonly marked with biological sisters, cousins, sisters in law and close friends. Q. How is Sisters Day celebrated? A. Usually with a message or social media post, a call, a small gift, or time spent together. There is no fixed way to observe it."}